1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,740
Hello everyone, this is Ria!

2
00:00:03,740 --> 00:00:08,930
Everyone, are you a bit tired right now?

3
00:00:08,930 --> 00:00:12,070
Or are you not tired?

4
00:00:12,070 --> 00:00:13,760
Are you okay?

5
00:00:13,760 --> 00:00:20,120
I've been traveling for quite a long time.

6
00:00:20,120 --> 00:00:24,860
Of course, traveling is fun.

7
00:00:24,860 --> 00:00:29,820
Everything is new and exciting.

8
00:00:29,820 --> 00:00:38,280
But honestly, sometimes traveling can be a bit tough.

9
00:00:38,280 --> 00:00:40,820
There are tough moments too.

10
00:00:40,820 --> 00:00:46,980
What do you find the most difficult when you travel?

11
00:00:46,980 --> 00:00:50,770
What is the hardest part when you travel?

12
00:00:50,770 --> 00:00:58,390
For me, the hardest thing was, um... sleep!

13
00:00:58,390 --> 00:01:03,000
I had a really hard time because of sleep.

14
00:01:03,000 --> 00:01:11,110
It was hard when I first arrived, and it's still a bit hard.

15
00:01:11,110 --> 00:01:16,090
I'm currently staying in a city.

16
00:01:16,090 --> 00:01:21,490
So there are too many people and it's noisy.

17
00:01:21,490 --> 00:01:22,530
It's noisy.

18
00:01:22,530 --> 00:01:27,480
Especially at dawn, it's very noisy.

19
00:01:27,480 --> 00:01:29,720
Motorcycle sounds

20
00:01:29,720 --> 00:01:33,020
Car horn sounds

21
00:01:33,020 --> 00:01:34,730
Music sounds

22
00:01:34,730 --> 00:01:37,470
People laughing

23
00:01:37,470 --> 00:01:40,220
Things like these can be heard.

24
00:01:40,220 --> 00:01:44,440
At night, it starts to get noisy.

25
00:01:44,440 --> 00:01:47,240
It starts to get noisy.

26
00:01:47,240 --> 00:01:54,970
I thought everyone would be sleeping at dawn.

27
00:01:54,970 --> 00:01:59,460
But it gets worse at dawn.

28
00:01:59,460 --> 00:02:01,420
It gets worse.

29
00:02:01,420 --> 00:02:05,660
What are they doing without sleeping?

30
00:02:05,660 --> 00:02:10,120
It's so noisy that I can't fall asleep.

31
00:02:10,120 --> 00:02:11,840
I can't fall asleep.

32
00:02:11,840 --> 00:02:22,660
Also, when I first arrived in Japan, it was hard to get used to the different bed.

33
00:02:22,660 --> 00:02:25,890
It was hard to get used to.

34
00:02:25,890 --> 00:02:33,410
When my sleeping place changes, I have trouble falling asleep.

35
00:02:33,410 --> 00:02:34,720
Sleeping place

36
00:02:34,720 --> 00:02:39,490
But do you know what's really funny?

37
00:02:39,490 --> 00:02:55,010
If you say 잠자리 (jamjari) in Korean with a steady tone, it means the insect "dragonfly" in English.

38
00:02:55,010 --> 00:02:56,920
Jamjari

39
00:02:56,920 --> 00:03:10,380
But if you pronounce '자' as '짜' in 잠자리, it refers to the atmosphere or environment of the place where you sleep.

40
00:03:10,380 --> 00:03:12,090
Jamjjari

41
00:03:12,090 --> 00:03:18,610
You can say something like "The sleeping place was a bit uncomfortable..."

42
00:03:18,610 --> 00:03:22,970
And there's something even worse.

43
00:03:22,970 --> 00:03:24,860
Something even worse!

44
00:03:24,860 --> 00:03:30,650
I'm currently staying with my older sister.

45
00:03:30,650 --> 00:03:35,710
But sometimes my sister snores.

46
00:03:35,710 --> 00:03:38,530
She snores.

47
00:03:38,530 --> 00:03:44,020
Because of that, sometimes I can't sleep well.

48
00:03:44,020 --> 00:03:48,000
There's an expression in Korean.

49
00:03:48,000 --> 00:03:52,770
잠귀가 밝다 (jamgwiga balda).

50
00:03:52,770 --> 00:03:58,860
잠 (jam) is the sleep you know,

51
00:03:58,860 --> 00:04:03,940
and 귀 (gwi) is this ear on my face.

52
00:04:03,940 --> 00:04:12,450
Combining sleep + ear makes '잠귀' (jamgwi).

53
00:04:12,450 --> 00:04:13,250
Jamgwi

54
00:04:13,250 --> 00:04:24,510
So when you say "잠귀가 밝아요," it means a person who wakes up easily from small sounds while sleeping.

55
00:04:24,510 --> 00:04:27,390
A person who wakes up easily.

56
00:04:27,390 --> 00:04:28,740
Someone like me.

57
00:04:28,740 --> 00:04:33,560
I think I have a light sleep.

58
00:04:33,560 --> 00:04:42,590
I wasn't like this before, but lately my sleep sensitivity has... gotten a bit higher.

59
00:04:42,590 --> 00:04:45,470
My sleep sensitivity has increased.

60
00:04:45,470 --> 00:04:47,700
How about you?

61
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:59,100
There are many reasons why people can't sleep, but I'm especially sensitive to sound.

62
00:04:59,100 --> 00:05:01,410
I'm sensitive to sound.

63
00:05:01,410 --> 00:05:02,450
Sensitive.

64
00:05:02,450 --> 00:05:15,570
So when there's a loud noise outside the house or when my sister snores, I can't sleep deeply.

65
00:05:15,570 --> 00:05:18,260
I toss and turn in my sleep.

66
00:05:18,260 --> 00:05:30,050
"Tossing and turning" means waking up repeatedly during sleep or not sleeping well.

67
00:05:30,050 --> 00:05:37,020
But on the other hand, my sister is not very sensitive.

68
00:05:37,020 --> 00:05:38,650
Not sensitive.

69
00:05:38,650 --> 00:05:41,280
She's the opposite of me.

70
00:05:41,280 --> 00:05:43,470
Completely opposite.

71
00:05:43,470 --> 00:05:47,330
She sleeps very well.

72
00:05:47,330 --> 00:05:52,860
There's a perfect Korean expression for this.

73
00:05:52,860 --> 00:05:57,540
업어 가도 모른다 (eopeo gado moreunda).

74
00:05:57,540 --> 00:06:02,120
First, you need to know the word '업다' (eopda).

75
00:06:02,120 --> 00:06:07,460
'업다' means to carry someone on your back.

76
00:06:07,460 --> 00:06:16,800
In Korean dramas, there are many scenes where a man carries a woman on his back.

77
00:06:16,800 --> 00:06:25,250
But if someone carries you on their back while you're sleeping,

78
00:06:25,250 --> 00:06:28,290
carrying you away,

79
00:06:28,290 --> 00:06:30,660
and you don't even know it!

80
00:06:30,660 --> 00:06:35,740
You just keep sleeping on their back.

81
00:06:35,740 --> 00:06:40,380
How deeply must you be asleep to not notice that?

82
00:06:40,380 --> 00:06:46,910
That's why we use the phrase "업어 가도 모른다."

83
00:06:46,910 --> 00:06:51,690
For example, you can say this:

84
00:06:51,690 --> 00:06:55,500
Do you usually sleep well?

85
00:06:55,500 --> 00:07:03,030
Yes, once I fall asleep, I sleep very deeply.

86
00:07:03,030 --> 00:07:10,290
I think I wouldn't even know if someone carried me away.

87
00:07:10,290 --> 00:07:13,540
Such a cute expression, right?

88
00:07:13,540 --> 00:07:20,950
It refers to someone who can sleep anywhere.

89
00:07:20,950 --> 00:07:32,070
But if you didn't sleep well the night before, if you toss and turn, the next day is really hard.

90
00:07:32,070 --> 00:07:34,840
The next day is really hard.

91
00:07:34,840 --> 00:07:37,400
You get a bit sensitive.

92
00:07:37,400 --> 00:07:40,990
You feel lethargic.

93
00:07:40,990 --> 00:07:47,910
You don't want to do anything for no reason and feel blank all the time.

94
00:07:47,910 --> 00:07:49,600
This is "blank."

95
00:07:49,600 --> 00:07:52,930
Blank... feeling blank.

96
00:07:52,930 --> 00:08:04,510
So especially when traveling or when you have something important the next day, sleep really seems important.

97
00:08:04,510 --> 00:08:09,370
What do you do when you can't fall asleep?

98
00:08:09,370 --> 00:08:19,510
Usually, many people listen to ASMR when they can't sleep.

99
00:08:19,510 --> 00:08:28,880
I also tried listening to ASMR once before going to sleep.

100
00:08:28,880 --> 00:08:41,100
I searched for ASMR videos on YouTube and listened, but honestly, it wasn't very good.

101
00:08:41,100 --> 00:08:47,860
There are so many different kinds of ASMR videos.

102
00:08:47,860 --> 00:08:54,720
Roleplay videos acting like "Welcome~"

103
00:08:54,720 --> 00:08:57,590
Water sound videos

104
00:08:57,590 --> 00:09:00,880
Sounds of touching objects

105
00:09:00,880 --> 00:09:06,440
I tried all these videos but they weren't good.

106
00:09:06,440 --> 00:09:12,580
Rather, I couldn't sleep more.

107
00:09:12,580 --> 00:09:18,690
I think it's because I'm sensitive to sound.

108
00:09:18,690 --> 00:09:25,920
I really need it to be quiet and calm to fall asleep well.

109
00:09:25,920 --> 00:09:28,600
Quiet, calm.

110
00:09:28,600 --> 00:09:36,550
If you're curious about the detailed difference between these, please click the link!

111
00:09:36,550 --> 00:09:50,290
Anyway, a while ago, I saw a comment from a subscriber saying they listen to my podcast before going to sleep.

112
00:09:50,290 --> 00:09:54,340
Seeing that made me really happy!

113
00:09:54,340 --> 00:10:11,210
I'm sensitive to sound, so I don't listen to anything when I sleep... but it's so sweet that a subscriber listens to my voice to fall asleep.

114
00:10:11,210 --> 00:10:12,890
So sweet.

115
00:10:12,890 --> 00:10:19,800
"So sweet" is English, but many Koreans use it a lot.

116
00:10:19,800 --> 00:10:23,390
So sweet! They say it a lot like this.

117
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:28,420
Um... and another way when you can't fall asleep!

118
00:10:28,420 --> 00:10:33,590
I use earplugs like this.

119
00:10:33,590 --> 00:10:37,980
This is my essential item when traveling.

120
00:10:37,980 --> 00:10:39,810
Essential item!

121
00:10:39,810 --> 00:10:45,820
I learned this expression a long time ago, does anyone remember?

122
00:10:45,820 --> 00:10:48,620
I praise you, clap clap clap!!!

123
00:10:48,620 --> 00:10:59,250
I use it on planes and often when it's noisy like where I live now.

124
00:10:59,250 --> 00:11:04,780
In high school, I used it often when studying.

125
00:11:04,780 --> 00:11:09,500
But sometimes I forget to bring it.

126
00:11:09,500 --> 00:11:12,260
Sometimes I forget.

127
00:11:12,260 --> 00:11:16,180
Sometimes I forget and can't bring it.

128
00:11:16,180 --> 00:11:25,360
Every time that happens, I say "Ah... I'm doomed, I'm doomed," and do you know what I do?

129
00:11:25,360 --> 00:11:28,030
I sleep with earphones.

130
00:11:28,030 --> 00:11:33,120
I sleep with noise-canceling earphones.

131
00:11:33,120 --> 00:11:37,500
It's a bit uncomfortable for my ears.

132
00:11:37,500 --> 00:11:42,900
It's uncomfortable, but it's better than the noise.

133
00:11:42,900 --> 00:11:47,870
Sleep is important for everyone.

134
00:11:47,870 --> 00:11:51,200
Sleep is the most important.

135
00:11:51,200 --> 00:11:56,280
I think sleep is the most important.

136
00:11:56,280 --> 00:12:02,370
There's a slang word in Korean called '꿀잠' (kkuljam).

137
00:12:02,370 --> 00:12:03,780
Kkuljam

138
00:12:03,780 --> 00:12:11,600
It's slang, but it's a cute slang, so even adults use it a lot.

139
00:12:11,600 --> 00:12:14,400
How does honey taste?

140
00:12:14,400 --> 00:12:17,570
Honey is very sweet.

141
00:12:17,570 --> 00:12:19,520
Very sweet.

142
00:12:19,520 --> 00:12:27,140
So usually when '꿀' (honey) is added in front of Korean slang, it has a good meaning.

143
00:12:27,140 --> 00:12:33,340
'꿀잠' means good sleep, pleasant sleep.

144
00:12:33,340 --> 00:12:47,730
So in Korean, there are expressions like "잘 자요, 잘 자" (sleep well), but you can also say "꿀잠 자세요, 꿀잠 자요" (have a sweet sleep).

145
00:12:47,730 --> 00:12:56,250
I hope from now on, you and I all have sweet sleep.

146
00:12:56,250 --> 00:13:04,060
If you have any sweet sleep tips(?), please let me know in the comments!

147
00:13:04,060 --> 00:13:13,730
Then, wishing everyone a sweet sleep tonight, I'll end the video.

148
00:13:13,730 --> 00:13:18,190
See you next time with more fun stories.

149
00:13:18,190 --> 00:13:22,620
Sleep well! Have a sweet sleep :)
